---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Voice" description="What Grok Voice is: spoken interaction, voices, and connectors in voice mode.">
  <section class="about-content">
    <p class="home-kicker" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Features</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Voice</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle muted">Spoken interaction with Grok across platforms.</p>
    <p><strong>Voice</strong> is how users speak to Grok instead of only typing. It is an interaction mode on top of the same <a href="/models">models</a>, designed for conversation, hands-free use, and — when connectors are enabled — spoken access to external tools.</p>
    <h2>Platforms and voices</h2>
    <p>Official announcements have described Voice features across iOS, Android, and web, and have introduced additional voice options on those platforms.</p>
    <h2>Connectors in voice mode</h2>
    <p><strong>Connectors</strong> are how Grok reaches external tools and accounts. Official updates have stated that connectors can be used while in voice mode, not only in typed chat.</p>
    <h2>What Voice is for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Spoken conversation with Grok on supported apps and the web</li>
      <li>Choosing among available voices</li>
      <li>Using connectors during voice sessions when enabled</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Voice vs other products</h2>
    <p>Voice is a mode of interaction. <a href="/imagine">Imagine</a> is media generation. <a href="/bot">Grok Bot</a> is teammate-style agency. <a href="/build">Grok Build</a> is a coding/agentic harness.</p>
    <h2>How Grokati covers Voice</h2>
    <p>We publish sourced updates when official accounts change platform availability, voice catalogues, or connector-in-voice behaviour.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a href="/features">← All features</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>